<title>PORTUGAL: Beta Finance issues 5 bln esc 6.85 pct Navigator.</title>
<headline>Beta Finance issues 5 bln esc 6.85 pct Navigator.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Beta Finance Corporation has launched a five billion escudo five-year Navigator bond issue at a fixed rate of 6.85 percent, joint leaders Citibank Portugal (bookrunner) and Citibank International Plc said.</p>
<p>Issuer: Beta Finance Corporation</p>
<p>Type: part of programme of medium term notes of issuer</p>
<p>Rating:AAA/Aaa		  Nominal value: 5 billion escudos</p>
<p>Interest rate: 6.85 percent Launch date: 9 October 1996</p>
<p>Maturity: 30 October 2001   Payment: 30 October 1996</p>
<p>Price of issue: 100.00 percent</p>
<p>Price of reimbursement: 100.00 percent</p>
<p>Payment of interest: on October 30 each year</p>
<p>Admission to quotation: London stock exchange</p>
<p>Legislation: British law</p>
<p>Joint leaders: Citibank Portugal (bookrunner) and Citibank</p>
<p>International Paying agent: Citibank Portugal</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
